As noted in the June 2026 Release notes under tickets WSP-3980, WSP-3982, a=
nd WSP-4043

Enhancement to Employee Details Form -
A new field, International Employee, now displays on the Address tab in the=
 Employee Details form.
For example:
[https://tech-docs.prismhr.com/SP_help/Content/Resources/Images/PD/Release-=
Notes/International_Employee_field_Address_tab_Employee_Details_form.png ]<=
https://tech-docs.prismhr.com/SP_help/Content/Resources/Images/PD/Release-N=
otes/International_Employee_field_Address_tab_Employee_Details_form.png >
Note: This feature is only available for service providers. To use this fea=
ture, you must enable the system-level INTLEMPLOYEE custom feature code on =
the System Parameters form.
To waive requiring a US-based resident address for an international employe=
e, select International Employee.
Note the following:

  *
After clicking Save a warning displays if the employee was paid in the past=
 (that is, the Last Pay Date contains a date), "Warning: Employee records w=
ith pay data cannot be saved as International Employees."
  *
After clicking Save a warning displays if the employee was not paid in the =
past (that is, the Last Pay Date is blank), "Warning: International Employe=
es cannot be processed in a payroll batch, as they do not have a resident a=
ddress. Would you like to proceed?" Click Yes to proceed. The record saves =
without requiring Resident Address information. (If appropriate, select Int=
ernational Address and enter the employee's international address in the Ma=
iling Address panel.)
  *
After selecting International Employee, data in the Address, ZIP Code, City=
, State, County, and Geocode fields clear.
  *
When the following occurs during payroll processing:
=95
An employee has hours on a calculated payroll
=95
The employee record is then updated to an International Employee
=95
The calculated payroll is finalized without recalculation
The system displays a payroll error message and stops payroll finalization,=
 then one of the following scenarios occurs:
=95
If you disable the International Employee field from the employee record an=
d attempt finalizing the payroll again, the system allows the payroll final=
ization process to complete successfully.
=95
If you remove the International Employee pay from the timesheet, the system=
 allows you to recalculate and refinalize the payroll successfully (assumin=
g there are no other errors).
=95
If you recalculate the payroll with the International Employee field enable=
d, the system displays a calculation error because there is no resident add=
ress for the International Employee and payroll finalization is no longer a=
n available option in the payroll process.





